xnu 0300: the touch reports its contacts as coming from a screen edge

iOS only starts the home and app-switcher gestures for a touch that UIKit
knows began at a display edge. Apple's touch firmware marks such a contact
with kIOHIDDigitizerEventFromEdgeTip for its whole life and UIKit derives
UITouch's edge type from it (_UIEventHIDTouchEdgeTypeForHIDEvent). The
mondrian event never set the bit, so SpringBoard saw an ordinary finger
everywhere: an app could be opened, but no swipe from the bottom edge ever
left it.

A contact that starts within ~3 mm of any panel edge now carries the bit
until it lifts. The identity bit is also only set on the first down, not on
the lift, matching the event the reference driver produces.

diff --git a/iokit/Kernel/arm/hid/MondrianHID.cpp b/iokit/Kernel/arm/hid/MondrianHID.cpp
--- a/iokit/Kernel/arm/hid/MondrianHID.cpp
+++ b/iokit/Kernel/arm/hid/MondrianHID.cpp
@@ -363,6 +363,14 @@
  * absolute digitizers.
  */
 #define MONDRIAN_TOUCH_FINGERS 10
+/*
+ * Contacts that start this close to a panel edge (0.1 px units, ~3 mm) carry
+ * kIOHIDDigitizerEventFromEdgeTip for their whole life, as Apple's touch
+ * firmware reports them. UIKit derives UITouch's edge type from that bit
+ * (_UIEventHIDTouchEdgeTypeForHIDEvent); without it there is no home or
+ * app-switcher gesture.
+ */
+#define MONDRIAN_TOUCH_EDGE 640
 class MondrianHIDTouch : public IOHIDEventService {
 	OSDeclareDefaultStructors(MondrianHIDTouch);
 public:
@@ -386,6 +394,7 @@
 	UInt32 fLoggedClients;   /* client count last printed */
 	UInt32 fEvents;          /* events dispatched */
 	bool fDown[MONDRIAN_TOUCH_FINGERS];
